    <div class="flow-step"><b>Discover</b><span>Match subject and object forms.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Build</b><span>Replace repeated nouns and things.</span></div>
    <div class="flow-step"><b>Use</b><span>Track people and things in a fictional task.</span></div>
  </div>

  <p class="note-line">Object pronouns keep your sentences short and natural: say a name once, then let <span class="ex">me, him, her, it, us,</span> and <span class="ex">them</span> do the work.</p>

  <h2>Two-minute retrieval</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="practice" data-choice-gap-drill data-success-message="Correct. You retrieved a subject pronoun, a possessive adjective, and third-person present-simple agreement.">
    <h3>Three quick checks from earlier lessons</h3>
