  <h2>Notice and repair errors</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="she" data-hint="The pronoun comes after saw and refers to the person who receives the seeing action." data-fix="I saw her at the market." data-why="After a verb, use the object form: saw her.">
    <h3>Drill 6: object after the verb</h3>
    <p>The previous sentence introduced Elena with <span class="ex">she</span>. Tap the word that is wrong in “I saw she at the market.”</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="i">I</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="saw">saw</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="she">she</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="market">at the market.</button>
    </div>
    <p class="hidden-answer" data-error-feedback></p>
  </div>

  <div class="micro-drill" data-spot-error data-answer="he" data-hint="The pronoun follows the preposition to, so it needs the object form." data-fix="Listen to him carefully." data-why="After the preposition to, use the object form: to him.">
    <h3>Drill 7: object after a preposition</h3>
    <p>The speaker card introduced Omar with <span class="ex">he</span>. Tap the word that is wrong in “Listen to he carefully.”</p>
    <div class="spot-options">
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="listen">Listen</button>
      <button class="error-choice" data-error-choice="to">to</button>
