  <h2>Use it in real life</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <p class="note-line">You never need to disclose your real family, contacts, messages, phone use, workplace, relationships, schedule, or location. Use the fictional staff cards, project files, help desk, or event plan below whenever you prefer.</p>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Role swap:</b> Use two fictional staff cards to show a subject and object changing roles. <span class="ex">She helps him. He helps her.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Known project items:</b> Introduce one file and several photos, then continue with <span class="ex">it</span> and <span class="ex">them</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Help desk:</b> Make three requests with an object after a verb or preposition. <span class="ex">Call me. Wait for us. Send it to them.</span></div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>One unknown visitor:</b> Introduce one person without specifying <span class="ex">he</span> or <span class="ex">she</span>, then refer back with singular <span class="ex">them</span>.</div>
  <div class="prompt-card"><b>Clear reference:</b> Create one unclear sentence with two possible references. Repeat a name or noun to make the intended person unmistakable.</div>

  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Final production: coordinate a fictional community event</h3>
    <p>Give a 45–60 second staff and materials update. Include all six pieces of evidence:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>one role swap with a subject form and its object partner;</li>
      <li>one object directly after a verb and one after a preposition;</li>
      <li><span class="ex">it</span> for one known item and <span class="ex">them</span> for several known items;</li>
      <li>singular <span class="ex">them</span> for one person whose <span class="ex">he / she</span> pronoun is not specified;</li>
      <li>one natural placement such as <span class="ex">Send it to her</span>;</li>
      <li>one linked neutral pronoun and one contrastively stressed pronoun: <span class="ex">Call <strong>ME</strong>, not them</span>.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The listener identifies every pronoun’s reference. If any pronoun could point to two people or things, revise the update by repeating the clearest name or noun.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Reflect</h2>
  <div class="lead-rule"></div>
  <div class="thinking-card">
    <h3>Say the system back</h3>
    <p>Recite the seven pairs aloud: <span class="ex">I → me, you → you, he → him, she → her, it → it, we → us, they → them.</span> Then complete this aloud: “Before the verb, I use the ______ form. After the verb or a preposition, I use the ______ form.”</p>
    <p>Then use two fictional staff cards to say one subject sentence, one object-after-verb sentence, and one object-after-preposition sentence.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="quiz" data-quiz data-success-message="Correct. You matched object forms to explicit roles and clear singular, plural, speaker, and thing references.">
